-> What is routing?

routing = route
Routing is process of selecting path for data to travel from one point to another. Routing figure out the best way to get from A to B
Devices called routers decide where data should go next. They use rules, tables, or algorithms to choose the best path

In frontend development, routing means deciding which content or page to show when the user navigates to a specific URL without necessarily reloading the whole website.

Routing = mapping a URL → to a UI (component/page)
/ → Home page
/about → About page
/profile → Profile page

In modern apps (React or Vue.js), routing is usually handled on the client side called Client-Side Routing
The page doesn’t fully reload, JavaScript updates only the needed part of the UI, making apps faster and smoother

import { BrowserRouter, Routes, Route } from "react-router-dom";
function App() {
  return (
    <BrowserRouter>
      <Routes>
        <Route path="/" element={<Home />} />
        <Route path="/about" element={<About />} />
      </Routes>
    </BrowserRouter>
  );
}

Server-side routing: Server sends a new HTML page for each URL, Traditional websites

New frameworks like Next.js combine both:
First page → server-side (fast + SEO)
Navigation → client-side (smooth UX)
