-> writing clean and maintainable code, what it mean and how can you do it!

“writing clean, maintainable code”, it means writing code that is easy to read, understand, and modify—not just code that works. This is super important in real-world projects where teams collaborate and software evolves over time.

-> Meaningful names: Variables, functions, and classes should describe their purpose
-> Keep functions small: Each function should do one thing only
-> Avoid repetition
-> Consistent formatting
-> Error handling (try-catch): Handle errors gracefully instead of crashing the app
