-> delivering responsive and user-friendly interfaces

1) Responsive means your app adapts to any device or screen size—desktop, tablet, or mobile

This is DONE by:
a) CSS Media Queries – adjust layout for screen size
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .container {
    flex-direction: column;
  }
}
b) Flexible grids & layouts – use percentages or CSS Grid/Flexbox
c) Responsive images – <img srcset> or CSS object-fit

2) User-friendly means the app is intuitive, easy to use, and enjoyable
a) Clear navigation
b) Fast loading 
c) Consistent design – buttons, colors, fonts, and spacing
d) Feedback & accessibility – e.g., hover effects, error messages, screen reader support
Example: A “Submit” button changes color on click and shows a spinner while the request is processing
